# `domain` module

Innermost boundary. Zero framework dependencies.

## Allowed dependencies

None. This is the core — it knows no other module.

## Forbidden in this module

- `org.springframework..`
- `jakarta.persistence..`
- `jakarta.validation..`
- `com.fasterxml.jackson..`
- `tools.jackson..`

Whoever writes them, the CI job `architectural boundaries` fails on them: its
`ArchHook.java doctor gate` sweeps every source file against `.claude/forbidden-imports.txt`.
Under Claude Code the `check` hook also blocks them at edit time. If you need one of these, the
responsibility is in the wrong module — move the code, not the rule.

## Base package

`com.exemplo.minhaapi.domain`

Full rule: `.claude/rules/architecture-ddd.md`
